  {
   "access_tier": "public",
   "codebook_declared_type": "text",
   "description": "WHICH FEDERAL PROGRAMME'S GEOGRAPHY A ROW BELONGS TO, and the column to read before comparing any two regions. `BIA_REGION`, `BIA_AGENCY`, `IHS_AREA`, `IHS_SERVICE_UNIT`, `NIGC_REGION`, `HUD_ONAP_AREA`. A tribe sits in several of these at once and their boundaries do not align, so there is no universal region. The same word can name different ground in different systems - `Phoenix` is an IHS area, an NIGC region and a HUD office location, and is not a BIA region at all.",
   "examples": [
    "BIA_REGION",
    "BIA_AGENCY",
    "IHS_AREA",
    "IHS_SERVICE_UNIT",
    "HUD_ONAP_AREA"
